# counter harness. One force call is one ASE calculate on the harness Lennard-Jones calculator.
# Local steps are SciPy L-BFGS-B stopped on the ASE maximum atomic force.
# The genetic algorithm follows the AGOX tests_ea script: population 10, SimpleFingerprint, and DistanceComparator with threshold 0.5. The archived geometry starts in the population. The first iteration draws 9 random structures, so the population stays at 10. From iteration 5 the schedule is 2 random and 8 rattles, and from iteration 10 it is 10 rattles. The rattle matches agox/lj38-bh, one quarter of the atoms at amplitude 3 Å. The script default rattles 3 atoms. Local optimization, seed, potential, success window, and cap are the same as agox/lj38-bh. The reference energy is the Cambridge cluster coordinates evaluated with this potential.
